Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
 Subject: Patching kernel rk35xx files drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c

Enable RK_PCIE_DBG as recommended by the Rockchip PCIe Developer Guide
section 13.2: when link training fails, the driver dumps the LTSSM
state and 64 lines of fifo_status (low two digits = LTSSM state
machine, see guide appendix 14.1) for every link attempt. Needed to
diagnose the JM10 PCIe 3.0 x4 slot bring-up.

Drop this patch once the slot works; it only prints during link
training, but the fifo dump is verbose.

Signed-off-by: John Doe <john.doe@somewhere.on.planet>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
@@ -35,5 +35,5 @@
 #include "../../../regulator/internal.h"
 
-#define RK_PCIE_DBG			0
+#define RK_PCIE_DBG			1	/* JM10 debug: LTSSM/fifo dump per guide 13.2 */
 
 #define PCIE_DMA_OFFSET			0x380000
 

